WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
Vladimir Putin's one.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:01.601
Ukraine

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.104
is certainly not going as he intended.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.306
But on the home front,

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.441
his dreams may be coming true.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.010
That was the thrust of a terrific

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.878
New York Times article by the paper's

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.047
Moscow reporters, Valerie Hopkins

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.249
and Anton Tryon Off Ski.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.451
Valerie joins me now from Moscow.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.587
Welcome Valerie.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.789
I want to ask you to start

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.057
by talking about something

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.026
that I found very interesting

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:26.960
in reporting

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.661
you've done before this article,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.864
but including this article

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.533
which is President Biden

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.969
has said a couple of times, I think

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.738
once the body bags start coming back,

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.908
the Russian people will stop supporting

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.444
this war or words to that effect.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.746
And what you found

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.949
is that the body bags are coming back,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.319
but it is actually increasing the support

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.655
for the war. Explain what's going on.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:58.725
Well, thank you very

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.260
much, Fareed, for having me.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.895
And I wish I didn't

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.563
have to talk about this with you today.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.399
But it's true in my reporting

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.967
across Russia.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.935
What I found

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:09.502
when talking

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.837
to people, mothers of

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.639
of those who who have been lost

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.942
or relatives, people are finding that

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.211
their losses are actually making them

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.113
support the war even more.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.182
They're starting to feel it even more.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:22.715
And, of course,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.684
the Kremlin has refused

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.019
to actually release

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.121
the full statistical data

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.190
of how many people have been killed,

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.259
how many soldiers have died in this war.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:33.793
You know,

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.928
they've only released them

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:35.628
intermittently.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.963
And I believe the last full count

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.998
was in September at 6000.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.667
While Western intelligence

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.001
estimates that there have been

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.938
200,000 killed and wounded in this war.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.540
Russians only so,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.175
of course, many Russians.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:49.742
Most Russians

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.277
don't know the full extent of this.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.012
But my reporting

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.347
and reporting by other colleagues

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.715
who remain in Russia

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.983
and who have spoken to

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:57.550
to the mothers

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.085
and relatives of these dead soldiers

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.121
find that

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.755
that this makes them supportive of it

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.257
even more because,

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:04.958
you know,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.993
they feel a concrete sense of loss.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.729
They do believe they the propaganda

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.030
that that the government

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.831
has been pushing,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.032
not only for the past year,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.833
but also before,

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.902
but it has really ramped up

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.703
this year

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.772
is that the West seeks to destroy Russia.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.008
And this is an existential struggle

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.943
for Russia's survival against the West.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.845
And they also are increasingly

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.982
buying the line that actually the West

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.717
was preparing an invasion

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.153
and that Putin was smart

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.420
to take a preemptive

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.789
to preemptively invade Ukraine.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.359
It's quite surprising and quite shocking.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.894
But but this is where we are right now,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.561
one year in.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.897
You talk also about

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:44.297
a much

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.665
broader transformation

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.667
that is taking place in Russia.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.002
This goes back a long way,

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.636
the debate

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.570
between Russia,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.772
between the kind of Western eyes, ears

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.140
and what used to be called

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.542
the SLAVA files

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.409
you know, people who thought

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.511
Russia's destiny lies with the West

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.179
and those

00:02:59.179 --> 00:02:59.612
who said no,

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.681
Russia is its own distinct, unique

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.184
creature.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.553
You say that this war has helped

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.989
almost finally in a very decisive way.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.358
Move that debate in one direction, right?

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:14.594
Absolutely.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.596
Well, as you read in the article,

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.331
one of the very

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.832
one of the businessmen

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.601
closest to very close to President

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.571
Putin comes in military have expressed

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.939
his joy

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.074
that this war or his moment,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.243
he expressed some degree of closure,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.311
we can say,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.580
about the fact that this war continues

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.881
as long as it did know.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.050
As as you know,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.585
initially when this was planned,

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.019
it was planned as a blitzkrieg.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:40.286
It was

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.354
they thought they could take

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.188
Kiev in three

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:42.889
days,

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.523
change that,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.059
change the government and just occupy.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.393
But instead,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:47.727
you know,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.695
this has required

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.163
a societal transformation

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.564
and consulting mafia.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.499
This businessman said this is great.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.334
Because, you know,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.035
if the blitzkrieg had succeeded,

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:56.803
we would still have

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.905
these liberal elements of our society.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.440
But now that the longer it goes

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.507
on, the more

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.176
this changes into the society,

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.277
that Putin wants,

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.212
the more liberals are either silenced

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.947
or forced to flee.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.316
The more free speech is suppressed

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.385
and the more

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.088
it's possible to to create educational,

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.290
cultural institutions

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.726
and and even civil society

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:23.563
into the type of organizations and bodies

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.231
that the Kremlin wants to see,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.800
which are traditional conservative

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.869
and essentially define themselves

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:30.103
as the

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.704
antithesis to the values

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.107
that the West professes to stand for.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.575
So in a sense,

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.409
it feels to me

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.577
like what you're saying, the longer

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.178
this war goes on,

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:42.081
don't expect Russia to feel that it's,

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.449
oh, my goodness, it's a big mistake.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.951
It's actually having the effect

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:48.421
of making Russians double down on this

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.923
anti Western narrative and anti

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.191
Western society

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:54.360
On the one

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.094
hand, yes, I

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.963
think, you know, in the near term,

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.399
that's that is the case.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.233
But I think, you know,

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:00.933
what we've learned

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.168
from Russia's experience

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:02.769
with other wars,

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:03.236
you know,

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.337
the Russian and the Soviet

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.039
invasion of Afghanistan

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:06.939
was something

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.374
that many people were frustrated

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.409
about and opposed to.

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.076
But it didn't

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.245
it took them years to organize

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:15.248
and to truly be fed up and frustrated.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.717
I think a lot of this is actually apathy,

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.652
and much of that is due

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.119
to the fact

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.387
that the economy

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.457
has sort of more or less remained normal.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.591
But it's possible

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.160
that, you know, at a certain point

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:27.794
that there

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.095
there may be some tipping point.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.097
It's just how far along that might be.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.231
It's really hard to say.

